# Renders.
#
# Both bin/glitchvape and bin/glitchvape-batch default their output here, so
# this fills with megabytes on the first run and with hundreds of megabytes
# after an afternoon of --all-presets. Nothing in it is source: every file is
# reproducible from its seed and the settings that produced it.
#
# Unanchored, so a batch run started from a subdirectory is caught too.
out/

# Source photographs.
#
# The input side of the same coin, and not the program's to distribute.
Pictures/

# Bundled typefaces.
#
# Twenty-odd megabytes, and the licences are the fonts' own rather than this
# project's -- VCR OSD Mono and W95FA in particular are free to use but not
# obviously free to redistribute inside somebody else's repository.
#
# The program degrades correctly without them: GlitchVape::Fonts falls back
# through each role's candidate list to whatever fontconfig can see, and
# --check-fonts names the apt package or the download for anything still
# missing. See "Optional fonts" in the README for what to put here.
assets/fonts/

# Artwork is deliberately NOT ignored: assets/artwork/logo.png is a few
# kilobytes, is this project's own, and the about window needs it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by the tools this project is checked with

# perltidy leaves a .bak when it is run without the -bext='/' that the
# Makefile-less workflow in the README uses, writes a .ERR beside any file it
# could not parse, and a .LOG when asked for one.
*.bak
*.ERR
*.LOG
*.tdy

# prove --state
.prove

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local tooling and editors

# Claude Code keeps shared settings in .claude/settings.json and personal ones
# -- permission grants, machine-specific paths -- in the .local.json beside
# it. Only the personal half is ignored, so a shared config can still be
# committed if there is ever a reason to.
.claude/settings.local.json

.vscode/
.idea/

*~
*.swp
*.swo

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
